          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 25-year-old non-pregnant woman presents with dysuria and urinary frequency but</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 25-year-old non-pregnant woman presents with dysuria and urinary frequency but no fever or flank pain. Urine dipstick is leucocyte esterase positive. What is the most appropriate first-line empiric treatment?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ciprofloxacin 500 mg BD × 3 days</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Fluoroquinolones are second-line for uncomplicated cystitis due to rising resistance rates and the risk of collateral ecological damage; reserve them for complicated UTI or pyelonephritis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Amoxicillin 500 mg TDS × 7 days</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Amoxicillin has high resistance rates among common uropathogens (E. coli) in the Indian community and is not recommended as empiric first-line therapy for uncomplicated cystitis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Meropenem 1 g IV BD × 5 days</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Carbapenems are reserved for multi-drug resistant or complicated infections; using a carbapenem for uncomplicated cystitis is inappropriate and fuels carbapenem resistance.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Nitrofurantoin 100 mg modified-release BD × 5 days</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Nitrofurantoin achieves high urinary concentrations with minimal systemic absorption, has low resistance rates in India, and is the preferred first-line agent for uncomplicated cystitis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "For uncomplicated lower UTI in a young non-pregnant woman, nitrofurantoin 100 mg MR BD × 5 days is first-line. It is contraindicated only when eGFR is <30 mL/min."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Excellent. Nitrofurantoin is preferred because it concentrates in urine, spares the gut flora, and has low community resistance — key stewardship principles in action."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
